{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.CanonicalTitsIso","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CanonicalTitsIso","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CanonicalTitsIso.canonical_frame_c_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CanonicalTitsIso.canonical_frame_c_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/CanonicalTitsIso.lean#L43-L57","doc":"**The canonical (`*`-isometric) frame pins `c = 1`.** If the τ-intertwiner `T`\nrealises both the Schur proportionality `Tᵀ·G_Markov·T = c•G_Hodge` and the exact\n`*`-isometry `Tᵀ·G_Markov·T = G_Hodge` (the defining property of the canonical Tits\n`*`-iso, both forms canonically normalised), then `c = 1`. This is the sense in\nwhich the canonical Tits iso removes the μ²-gauge freedom of #4192: it is the\n`c = 1` frame. ","signatureChunk":0}]}